  "transcript": "A new aviation study has examined how airline crews avoid mistakes during takeoff. Before every major flight, pilots and their copilot run through a long safety checklist together. The study found that this simple habit catches small errors that could otherwise become serious problems. The checklist is updated every few years based on what airlines learn from real flights. Other industries are now starting to use similar checklists.",
